ry\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Lee County runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years. In 2025 that same pair ran 56% of normal on the middle of the grids, while July to August hit 144%. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 27% and March to April at 181%. Grid 25965 had its driest year in 2005 at 58%.</p>"}
